            "text": "Now I have a very thorough understanding of the flashblocks system. Let me also quickly check what the current RPC capabilities look like and what users interact with, then brainstorm features.\n\nLet me think about what improvements could be made for a flashblocks RPC node:\n\nThe current system:\n1. Receives flashblocks via WebSocket from the builder\n2. Builds pending blocks from flashblock sequences\n3. Exposes pending state via `eth_` RPC endpoints\n4. Has preconfirmation support (checking flashblocks for tx receipts)\n5. Has subscription APIs for flashblock events\n\nAreas for improvement brainstorming:\n\n\nOn the latency side, I could add flashblock-aware transaction submission that immediately returns preconfirmation status, implement streaming endpoints for real-time flashblock updates, precompute state roots in parallel, expose granular receipt data at the flashblock level, and warm up state caches for anticipated next blocks. For user experience, I should add dedicated RPC methods to query specific flashblocks, provide inclusion proofs, and build out transaction status tracking with flashblock-level granularity.\n\nFor reliability, I need multi-source flashblock ingestion from different builders, validation before serving to clients, health monitoring for the flashblock stream, and graceful fallback to standard blocks if flashblocks become unavailable. Performance-wise, I'm looking at parallel execution pipelines, streaming state diffs instead of full snapshots, a caching layer optimized for hot state, and batched delivery for catching up. Developer tools should include simulation APIs to test transactions against current flashblock state, event indexing, and debug/trace capabilities at flashblock granularity.\n\nNow I'm thinking through MEV protection features to round out the implementation.",
